Section 2) Aim:
To develop a Python program using Regular Expressions (Regex) to perform flexible product searches and display matching products.
Procedure:
Import the re module.
Enter the product list and search keyword.
Perform exact, prefix, suffix, partial, and case-insensitive searches using Regular Expressions.
Count and display the total number of matches for each search.
Stop.
Code:
import re
products = [
    "Apple iPhone",
    "Apple Watch",
    "Samsung Galaxy",
    "Galaxy Buds",
    "Dell Laptop",
    "HP Laptop",
    "Wireless Mouse",
    "Gaming Mouse"
]
keyword = "Apple"
# Exact Search
exact = [p for p in products if re.fullmatch(keyword, p, re.I)]
# Prefix Search
prefix = [p for p in products if re.match(keyword, p, re.I)]
# Suffix Search
suffix = [p for p in products if re.search(keyword + r"$", p, re.I)]
# Partial Search
partial = [p for p in products if re.search(keyword, p, re.I)]
print("Exact Search:", exact)
print("Prefix Search:", prefix)
print("Suffix Search:", suffix)
print("Partial Search:", partial)
print("\nReport")
print("Exact Matches:", len(exact))
print("Prefix Matches:", len(prefix))
print("Suffix Matches:", len(suffix))
print("Partial Matches:", len(partial))
